course: dictionary
lesson: 6148
title: Millilitres
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A millilitre, written ml, is a very small unit for measuring liquid. Juice, water and medicine are measured in millilitres. «A litre is 1000 millilitres (ml).» So a millilitre is one thousandth of a litre.
explain: A teaspoon holds about 5 millilitres, which helps you picture how small one millilitre is. When a problem gives litres, change them into millilitres by multiplying by 1000. «2 litres of juice is 2000 millilitres.»
explain: To find how many cups a drink fills, divide. «Cups of 250 millilitres hold it all in 2000 ÷ 250 = 8 cups.» Check your answer: 8 cups of 250 millilitres make 2000 millilitres, so it fits.
fact: A millilitre is a unit of volume, which means how much space a liquid takes up.
fact: 1000 millilitres make 1 litre.
fact: Millilitres are written ml or mL.
fact: A teaspoon holds about 5 millilitres, and a measuring cylinder in science is marked in millilitres.
fact: Medicine doses and drink cans are often labelled in ml.
exercise: How many millilitres are in 1 litre? | 500 | 100 | 10 | *1000
exercise: What is the short way to write millilitre? | *ml | kl | mg | mm
exercise: 2 litres of juice is how many millilitres? | 20 | 200 | 20000 | *2000
test: Turn 3 litres into millilitres. | 30 | 300 | *3000 | 30000
test: «Cups of 250 millilitres» fill 1000 millilitres. How many cups is that? | 2 | 25 | 5 | *4
exam: A carton holds 2 litres. You pour out 750 millilitres. How many millilitres are left? | 1500 | 2750 | *1250 | 1000
